{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidGroupNStrand","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovAxiomsPrimitive"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceN_from_inductive_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovTraceN_from_inductive_limit","kind":"instance","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L90-L105","doc":"**Inductive-limit ⇒ per-n** Markov-trace class. Under the\ninductive-limit class, every `MarkovTraceN n q` follows. Both\n`markovZax_legacy` (here) and `markovZN_legacy` (in\n`braid-group-n-strand`) are local copies of the Markov-Jones\nparameter `1/(√q + 1/√q)`; they are definitionally equal so the\n`tau_stab_factor_eq_z : tau_stab_factor = markovZN_legacy q` field\nis discharged by `rfl`. Both names are `@[deprecated]` — Phase 2\nmigrates this instance to the generic `markovZN (u : R)` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.defaultMarkovTraceInductiveLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.defaultMarkovTraceInductiveLimit","kind":"instance","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L75-L80","doc":"**Canonical instance** — placeholder discharging the class\ntrivially. The substantive content (per-n Markov-trace operators\n+ inductive-limit closure) is open R&D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.inclusion_residual_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.inclusion_residual_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The residual vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.inclusion_residual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.inclusion_residual","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Stabilisation residual: should be zero for the canonical\nJones-Wenzl trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTraceInductiveLimit","kind":"class","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L59-L70","doc":"**Inductive-limit Markov-trace compatibility.** The trace on the\n`n+1`-strand braid `ι_n(w) · σ_n` is the trace on `w` scaled by\nthe Markov-Jones parameter `z = 1/(√q + 1/√q)`.\n\n`inclusion_residual` is the scalar deviation; the class asserts\nit vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tauM_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tauM_n","kind":"opaque","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/markov-trace-inductive-limit.lean#L48-L51","doc":"The Markov trace `τ_M_n` on `n`-strand braid words at substrate\n`q`. Returns the scalar `ℝ` value. Concrete per-n discharges\nplug in via the per-n classes. ","signatureChunk":0}]}